# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. DESIGN SYSTEM & MOTION STANDARDS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

## Color Tokens (CSS Variables in main.css)
Default (Light-First Priority):
  --color-cerenkov:    #0284c7   ← Cerulean Blue primary accent
  --color-dissociation:#8b2f5a   ← Deep Rose secondary accent
  --color-alert:       #8b2f5a
  --color-abyssal:     #f7f5f0   ← Warm editorial background
  --color-graphite:    #eeebe3   ← Secondary structural background
  --text-primary:      #1a1612
  --text-secondary:    #5c5248
  --text-tertiary:     #7d736a

Dark Mode ([data-theme="dark"]):
  --color-cerenkov:    #00f0ff   ← Neon Cyan accent
  --color-dissociation:#ff0088   ← Neon Magenta accent
  --color-alert:       #ff0055
  --color-abyssal:     #050505   ← Deep dark background
  --color-graphite:    #1a1a1a   ← Secondary dark background
  --text-primary:      #e0e0e0
  --text-secondary:    #a0a0a0
  --text-tertiary:     #666666

## Core Motion Principle
All kinetic motion, accordion expansions, and interactive reveals are governed
by the unified Tubik 2026 spring curve:
  CSS Spring Token: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)

## Zero-Rigid-Pixels Mandate
Hardcoded `px` units for layout containers, section heights, and padding are
strictly forbidden. All geometry must use fluid scaling:
- Relative scaling: `rem`, `em`, `%`.
- Viewport dynamics: `vw`, `dvh` (accommodates mobile browser chrome).
- Fluid clamping: `clamp(min, preferred, max)`.
- Explicit container height token: `min-h-[clamp(26rem,55vh,36rem)]`.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. CORE SUBSYSTEM IMPLEMENTATIONS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

## Three.js WebGL Hero Orb (Dual-Mesh + Power Gating)
- Outer wireframe icosahedron (`IcosahedronGeometry(2.3, 2)`).
- Inner counter-rotating core (`IcosahedronGeometry(1.2, 1)`).
- Cursor parallax lerp.
- **Power Gating:** Managed via `IntersectionObserver`. Whenever the container
  exits the viewport, `requestAnimationFrame` is cancelled immediately (0% idle CPU).

## The Architectural Guide Spine
- Driven by GPU custom property `--scroll-progress` updated in a passive scroll listener.
- Optical thread connects Hero, Marquee, Accordion, Bento Grid, and Footer.

## Zone 4 Bento Grid Interactive Skill Matrix
- Asymmetric 12-column grid organized by stack layer:
  - Row 1: Backend & Data (8 cols) + DevOps & Infrastructure (4 cols)
  - Row 2: AI & Machine Learning (5 cols) + Frontend & WebGL (7 cols)
- Clickable skill pills update the context panel (`SKILL_DATA`) in `< 16ms`.
- Panel maintains an explicit fluid floor (`min-h-[clamp(6rem,12vh,8rem)]`) guaranteeing `CLS = 0`.
- Semantic `<button>` elements with `aria-pressed="true/false"` for total keyboard accessibility.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. CODING STANDARDS & CODE HYGIENE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

## Brand Sovereignty
- Always attribute **Lightoxy** as Loh Min Yu's crafted personal brand banner, never an agency or studio.
- Founder attribution: **Loh Min Yu (MinYuOuO)**.

## Strictly Prohibited Monikers
- Any legacy or retired personal aliases are permanently deprecated.
- Strictly ZERO occurrences of the retired moniker are permitted anywhere in code, comments, documentation, or commit messages (enforced by automated scanner).

## HTML & Link Standards
- Root landing page is `index.html`.
- All showcase deep-dives live in `pages/` (e.g. `pages/prms.html`).
- Static files live in `public/` (e.g. `public/CNAME`, `public/robots.txt`).
- Relative navigation: `pages/*.html` link back to `../index.html#projects`.
- Stylesheet link: `<link rel="stylesheet" href="/src/style/main.css">`.
- Script entry: `<script type="module" src="/src/script/main.js"></script>`.

## Development Workflow
1. Install: `npm install`
2. Dev Server: `npm run dev` (starts Vite with instant HMR)
3. Production Build: `npm run build` (Rollup multi-page compilation to `dist/` in < 400ms)
4. Local Preview: `npm run preview`
5. Automated CI/CD: Push to `main` triggers `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` which builds and deploys `./dist` to GitHub Pages (`minyu.my`).


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. WHAT NOT TO DO
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
- Do NOT use the retired personal moniker anywhere in the codebase.
- Do NOT use hardcoded pixel heights or widths (`px`) on layout containers.
- Do NOT re-introduce external CDN scripts (CDNJS, JSDelivr) for Three.js or GSAP; use local npm modules.
- Do NOT introduce heavy client-side SPA frameworks (React, Vue runtime, Angular).
- Do NOT create standalone output CSS files or run separate CLI watchers; Vite handles Tailwind v4 compilation natively.
- Do NOT place showcase HTML pages directly in the root directory; keep them in `pages/`.
- Do NOT place static deployment files (`CNAME`, `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`) directly in the root directory; maintain them in `public/`.
- Do NOT remove `IntersectionObserver` power gating from WebGL animation loops.
- Do NOT modify document identifiers or frontmatter schemas in `docs/` without conforming to `PORT-GOV-001`.
